  "notes": "The reward for quieting all six metronomes (src/game/practice-metronomes.js), heard once, in the wing, the first safe moment after the last one goes quiet. What the ticking was covering: the student through the partition, in exactly the order Source files it under STUDENT FILE (a scale, the correction tone, a faculty voice saying retain the reference, the same bar again after the room has emptied). Overheard first, then he can speak into the wall. The student has nothing of its own to say: every SIGNAL line quotes the rehearsal room. Nobody settles whether it is a person or the partition returning something once recorded there. The HUSH is only felt. Sounds are fired from main.js by line id (practiceStudentLine): scale, correction, bar, bar played sharp, knock, stop.",
  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "practice-wing.student.region",
      "title": "Through the wall",
      "kind": "scene",
      "color": "#2b2f36",
      "nodeIds": [
        "start",
        "wall",
